ukrainian tennis player leonid  stanislavski says he's too frightened to  leave his house in kharkiv in northeast  ukraine  russian bombs have landed close to his  home like millions of ukrainians his  life has been turned upside down by the  wall  just a few months ago the 97 year old  was celebrating after the guinness world  records named him the oldest competitive  tennis player in the world  when leonid was in spain competing in  the super seniors world championship he  played a friendly match against tennis  champion rafa nadal  it made headlines around the world  it was outstanding to meet him no one  could have imagined that so soon after  there would be war what has happened now  is simply horrible the world should do  everything it can to stop the war people  on both sides should not be dying while  others are standing  leonid has survived one world war he  worked as an engineer building warplanes  to fight the nazis his daughter is in  poland but he says it's too difficult  for him to get there so he'll stay in  kharkiv and wait for the fighting to  stop  i never thought that i would have to  live through another frightening war  where people on both sides are dying  mothers are losing their children wives  are losing their husbands it needs to be  stopped  before the russian invasion leonid  dreamed of playing against tennis star  roger federer  but now he only has one wish to survive  victoria gatenbee al jazeera
 

